{"name":"Chance of Rain","hex":"#a0a6a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opportunity or possibility.","Random occurrence; luck."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Happening by chance, casual."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chance"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Probability of precipitation","blocks":[{"text":"Probability of precipitation (PoP) is a commonly used term referring to the likelihood of precipitation falling in a particular area over a defined period of time, which is commonly a day, half day, or hour."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probability_of_precipitation","wikidata":"Q1564294"},{"title":"Chance of Rain (Laurel Halo album)","blocks":[{"text":"Chance of Rain is the second studio album by American electronic music artist Laurel Halo. The album was released on October 28, 2013, by Hyperdub and is Halo's second instrumental release of 2013, alongside her extended play Behind the Green Door. The album cover is the work of Halo's father, Arthur Chartow, drawn in the 1970s."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/56/Laurel_Halo_-_Chance_of_Rain_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chance_of_Rain_(Laurel_Halo_album)","wikidata":"Q16245439"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Konvektionsregen.jpg/500px-Konvektionsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Konvektionsregen.jpg/500px-Konvektionsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Convective precipitation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKonvektionsregen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Steigungsregen.jpg/500px-Steigungsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Steigungsregen.jpg/500px-Steigungsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orographic precipitation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASteigungsregen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Sturmfront_auf_Doppler-Radar-Schirm.jpg/500px-Sturmfront_auf_Doppler-Radar-Schirm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Sturmfront_auf